 "notes": "Primary source is the official LFP/ligue1.com 'International broadcasters' page (client-rendered; read via browser on 2026-10-26; no season label, but it reflects 2026-27 deals such as JioStar, Emtek-Vidio and XSports). LFP says Ligue 1 McDonald's is available in 215 territories via 53 broadcast partners in 44 languages for 2026-27. Domestic: Ligue 1+ is the sole broadcaster in France (all 306 matches); beIN SPORTS exited Ligue 1 domestically from 2026-27 (it remains a Ligue 2 BKT broadcaster). Free-to-air/free options: Brazil (CazéTV free stream, XSports FTA), China (CCTV-5), Malta (PBS), UK (ITV highlights only, may be outdated), Tajikistan (Varzish TV) and Uzbekistan (NTRC) - the last two inferred from state-broadcaster status. LFP also lists Sport 24 for ships and planes (in-flight/maritime, not a territory, omitted). No broadcaster listed by LFP for Australia, New Zealand, Greece, Hungary, Malaysia, Singapore, Philippines, Brunei, Cambodia, San Marino (Wikipedia marks these TBD). Wikipedia-only entries not on the LFP list (not included as entries): Laos (JAS), Suriname (STVS), Puerto Rico (beIN, grouped with US), Iran (Persiana Sports), Belarus (Kinopoisk), Brazil (CNN Brasil).",
